# Direct dependencies. requirements.txt is generated by `python -m harness.lock` and pins the
# full transitive set with a hash for every published file. Policy: every published file of
# every pin must be at least 14 days old at lock time (the LiteLLM 1.107.0 lesson).
# pySigma 1.5.1 + backend 2.0.0 were checked verdict-for-verdict against 2.0.1 + 2.1.1
# on 2026-10-23 and agree.
pySigma==1.5.1
pySigma-backend-sqlite==2.0.0
PyYAML==6.0.3

# pySigma requires diskcache only for sigma.data.mitre_attack and sigma.data.mitre_d3fend,
# which cache downloaded MITRE data. The harness never imports them (self-test 14 checks
# this), so the package is not installed at all. diskcache 5.6.3 has an unpatched
# advisory on pickle-based cache reads; leaving it out removes that code entirely.
# lock: exclude diskcache - only used by pySigma's MITRE data cache, which the harness never imports
# lock: exclude diskcache-stubs - type stubs for diskcache, unused at runtime

# certifi 2026.10.19 removes the emSign root CA whose intermediate CA keys were compromised
# (GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2, critical). It is younger than the 14-day cooldown, and a CA distrust
# cannot wait. The waiver covers only the wheel and sdist hashed below, so a file added to the
# release later still has to clear the cooldown. Remove the line once the release is 14 days
# old; the lock fails until you do.
# lock: allow-young certifi==2026.10.19 sha256:035c1e85572b141bf1c3a3eff0e33a8eb74917522f2559075ff8d2fea780a1ae,42d35340cc5b9ba78e818ddbff0c5b1c2b779de448a340fd1b989f5fa8670e1b - GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 (compromised emSign intermediate CA keys)
